| Han characters read as Japanese (state 2 of the Han script step)
| Han: Japanese

| This file is in the scrub file format, but it is a utf-8 file for editing purposes
| Comments start with vertical bar, space
| All other lines need two tildes.
| Following rules are derived from kanjidic2.xml
| Following rules are derived from JMdict_e.xml
| The standard program ships this script with no rules of its own: the Japanese reading keeps the Han characters as they are.
